inkcut-cpp (0.3.0-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Device setup: redesigned Connection tab with full serial parameters
    (data bits, parity, stop bits, hardware/software flow control) and
    auto-detected port list with a refresh button.
  * Removed CUPS printer transport from the UI (kept for legacy job JSON).
  * Driver presets now force a compatible Protocol; the Protocol combo is
    locked unless "Custom" is checked.
  * G-code: new "Solenoid PWM" lift mode for DIY plotters with a solenoid
    on the GRBL spindle pin — emits M3 S<down> on pen-down and M5 (or
    M3 S<up>) on pen-up. New "DIY · GRBL Solenoid PWM" preset.
  * G-code: optional Feed (mm/min) fields appended to every G1/G0.
  * Speed (VS/!V) label clarified to "Speed (cm/s)" with tooltip.
  * Control panel: Pen up / Pen down now correctly emit M3/M5 / lift
    G-code on the very first press (previously skipped a transition).
  * Device setup dialog inherits the main window size instead of
    maximizing on tablet profile; Connection tab packs cleanly without
    floating labels.
  * Full Polish/English translations refreshed via scripts/sync_translations.py.

 -- pratanczuk <pratanczuk@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 16 May 2026 23:35:00 +0200

inkcut-cpp (0.2.0-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Initial public release of the C++/Qt6 port of Inkcut.
  * SVG, DXF (libdxfrw) and bitmap (libpotrace) import.
  * HPGL, DMPL, GPGL, G-code, CAMM output protocols.
  * EN/PL translations.

